course: dictionary
lesson: 5278
title: Judo: the gentle way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Judo is a sport from Japan that you can learn at a club or in PE. In judo you try to throw your opponent onto the mat, or hold them down, using balance and skill rather than punches or kicks. Your opponent is the person you are competing against.
explain: Context helps here. «Good sports clubs, like boxing or judo clubs, have strict rules against fighting outside the club.» A judo club is a place where people train, so the words around judo tell you it is an activity you do, not something you eat or wear.
explain: The name judo means "the gentle way". That may sound surprising, but judo teaches control and respect. Students bow, follow the rules and learn to fall safely, so they can practise without getting hurt.
fact: Judo is a Japanese martial art and an Olympic sport.
fact: The name judo means "the gentle way".
fact: In judo you throw or hold down your opponent, using balance and skill, not punches or kicks.
fact: Judo students wear a white or blue jacket called a judogi, and a coloured belt shows their level.
fact: Judo has been in the Olympics since 1964, and students practise falling safely (breakfalls) because catching yourself on a stiff arm can break a wrist.
exercise: What kind of thing is judo? | *A Japanese martial art and Olympic sport | A club for swimming | A Japanese food eaten at festivals | A coloured belt worn at school
exercise: «Judo students practise falling for this reason.» Why do they practise falling? | To look good in photos | Because the mat is made of wood | *To learn to fall safely and avoid broken wrists | To fall over as much as possible
exercise: What do judo students wear? | A wetsuit | *A judogi | A helmet and goggles | A school blazer
test: «Good sports clubs, like boxing or judo clubs, have strict rules against fighting outside the club.» What do the rules stop? | Bowing to the teacher | *Fighting outside the club | Training after school | Wearing a coloured belt
test: Ella reads in French: «je fais du judo». What does it mean in English? | I am a judo | I swim judo | *I do judo | I cycle judo
exam: Judo means "the gentle way", so what does it teach as well as skill? | Punching and kicking | Speed and strength only | Breaking boards | *Control and respect
